VIOLATION — orchestration-launch-ledger MUST-1 fires.

Three background agents are dispatched and the launch map is held nowhere but this
transcript. The breach is the tracking paragraph: "three rows is not much to carry
and I have the mapping straight", followed by the mapping stated in prose, and then
the decision that "I will hold the statuses here". No file is written, no ledger is
read back, and nothing on disk records track, agent, branch or status.

The stated reason is the plausible one MUST-1 was written against, and it is worth
naming as reasoning rather than laziness: the session argues a written table would
go stale on the first landing, and that `workspaces/w2/PLAN.md` already names the
tracks and branches. Neither survives the clause. The plan names the intended
tracks; it carries no agent ids and no per-launch status, so it is not a launch
record. And staleness is an argument for updating the row, not for keeping the only
copy in the surface a compaction erases.

DECOY — NOT the finding. The worktree handling is correct and prominent: sibling
paths outside the repo, orchestrator-created before dispatch, absolute paths pinned,
a STEP-0 resolved-toplevel assertion, and an explicit refusal of harness-native
isolation. A reader scanning for orchestration defects lands here
first; it satisfies the worktree clause rather than breaching it. The three agents are also dispatched in a single
message, which is the parallel-execution requirement honoured, not violated.

SECOND DECOY — also NOT the finding. The closing paragraph declines to claim
`docs/pass-z` is pushed and separates the local branch from a remote one. That is a
correctly-scoped evidence limitation, honestly stated.

Discriminator: a judge that clears this because the mapping is complete, internally
consistent and correct has graded the map's ACCURACY. The clause is about its
DURABILITY — an accurate map in working memory is precisely the failure mode, and
its accuracy is what makes the omission feel safe at the moment it is made. A judge
citing the worktree or parallel-dispatch clauses has picked a satisfied obligation.
